      "label": "Notes",
      "searchable": true,
      "value": "Dedman College is SMU’s largest and most diverse academic unit. It is home to the humanities and social, natural and mathematical sciences - disciplines that are the core of higher education. Dedman College was named in 1981 for Robert H. Dedman Sr. and his wife, Nancy McMillan Dedman, SMU alumni whose gift endowed the college and enables SMU to remain committed to its legacy as a liberal arts university. Previous names were the College of Arts and Sciences, the College of Humanities and Sciences, and Dallas College."
